      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gravelbourg"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s Our Lady of the Assumption Cathedral and former convent are part of a National Historic Site of Canada since 1995.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gravelbourg"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Gravelbourg’s historic railway station, Gaiety Theatre, and courthouse are listed heritage sites, reflecting its 20th‑century growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gravelbourg"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The French‑language College Mathieu, a boarding school for francophone youth, has been a cultural pillar for four decades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gravelbourg"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s murals illustrate the Stations of the Cross and the life of Saint Philomena, echoing its Catholic heritage.",
